#![doc = r#"
TSL 1.0 generated SIMD API.

The opaque [`Simd`] and [`Mask`] facade is the stable, representation-neutral
Rust surface. [`profile`] is the stable lower-level primitive surface selected
from compile-target features. [`tsl_core`] and [`tsl_algorithm`] remain public
because generated lower-level signatures depend on them, but are advanced
substrates rather than representation-stable types.

Unsuffixed lower-level operations do exactly the requested work. An operation
whose caller precondition can cause undefined behavior is an `unsafe fn`; it
does not sanitize inputs. A generated `_checked` companion exists only when TSL
can validate the complete catastrophic precondition before invoking the
ordinary operation. It returns [`Result`] with [`PreconditionError`]. Valid
references and slices remain a caller obligation because Rust cannot validate
forged references.

@{checked_api_examples}
"#]
